john bolton was former president trump's  national security adviser and previously  served as  u.s ambassador to the united nations and  he joins us now ambassador good morning  thanks for being with us thank you for  having me  uh a lot to talk about but let's start  with cuba you've said the u.s  should show strong support for the cuban  people  do you believe the president should be  advocating for regime change there do  you see this  as a national security threat  uh yes i do look ev ever since the cold  war russia has had a significant  interest in what happens in  cuba they've used cuban surrogates in  places like venezuela to ensure the  chavez maduro dictatorship there i've  talked about the troika of tyranny in  the western hemisphere cuba venezuela  and nicaragua  i think these demonstrations in cuba  which uh  experts say go back to the early 1960s  in terms of the size and the  the spread all across the island i think  this shows real dissatisfaction not  with temporary circumstances but with  the regime itself  and i think we've got lots of cuban  americans who can have a lot of  suggestions about  how to put pressure on this regime and  let the cuban people have their freedom  back  uh ambassador i also want to ask you  about afghanistan because the biden  administration is pulling troops out  uh by the end of august we're going to  be out of uh be leaving afghanistan  you've said that that's a mistake across  the board  that war has cost by some estimates in  in excess of two trillion dollars  is the price of leaving going to be even  higher than that do you think  well i think that's the risk look not  all of that money was spent on  uh on actual military hostilities and  the reason we went into afghanistan was  very clear because we were attacked  on september the 11th the reason we've  stayed in afghanistan  for 20 years is not out of charity it's  not to make afghanistan a nicer place  it's not even principally to defend  the government of afghanistan it's to  defend american  civilians against another terrorist  attack now if we  when we withdraw and nato along with us  uh people are pretty confident that the  taliban are going to take back over  all or nearly all of afghanistan there's  a high likelihood that al qaeda and isis  will once again  take central sanctuary there and  threaten us with terrorist attacks  that's the cost we should be looking at  not not looking at what it is today but  what we  prevent what we have prevented by our  sustained presence there  you think we accelerate the risk of  another 911.  i think that's the prospect if the  taliban take back over and i don't know  any  serious observer who doesn't think they  will they've maintained their ties with  al qaeda  isis and other terrorist groups we  haven't even heard of yet  will take advantage of the isolation of  afghanistan  and set up bases there we're there as an  insurance policy to protect america this  is not  a charity project for afghanistan the  opponents of our being there  have treated it as if we're trying to  make afghanistan into the switzerland of  central asia  that's not the purpose the purpose is to  protect america there  rather than to have to protect it in the  streets and over the skies here  you mentioned the russian influence uh  in cuba i want to ask you  about uh the buy administration's  approach towards russia  uh his predecessor who you worked for  you said in an interview last year that  you believe vladimir putin putin thinks  he can play president trump like a  fiddle  do you think mr biden has had a better  approach  well i think they're still getting  warmed up but we have had a summit  between biden and putin biden supposedly  told putin to cut out the cyber attacks  that was followed by a significant  ransomware attack we don't know whether  biden has  taken retaliatory measures i certainly  hope he has in cyberspace  but i think our policy on russia is  still very ill defined and  cuba is not a place to give the russians  a break  what do you think the president should  be doing with mr putin's particularly on  cyber security  well i think he should be beefing up  american offensive cyber capabilities to  create  structures of deterrence against what  the russians are doing putin has played  a weekend very well this is a form of  asymmetric or hybrid warfare that they  wage against the united states  we need to do a lot more just with  respect to russia but with respect to  china  iran and others who are engaging us and  and we're not adequately prepared  former uh former president trump uh your  former boss  uh won the straw poll at the cpac  conference  uh i think you got 70 percent of the  vote um  the only person who was even close to  that was ron desantis with 21  would you vote for president trump in  the next election or  for governor desantis  well i i don't think president trump's  going to run for re-election in 2024 he  may talk about it incessantly before  then  but i've had two polls that my super pac  has done already one national poll one  in new hampshire that shows  trump's support among his base within  the republican party  slipping which i don't think is  receiving adequate coverage  and i've got a poll coming out in the  next few days that will show  continuing splits and problems within  trump's base  i think trump's support is exaggerated  and i think people are making a mistake  if they think it's going to remain  durable so if  if he were the nominee though would you  support him  no and i didn't support him in 2020 i  don't think he's fit to be president  it would be a disaster for the  republican party to nominate him he  would lose  overwhelmingly he has very very little  support among  independents and he could take down an  awful lot of republican candidates for  the senate the house  and state and local elections ambassador  bolton thank you very much for being  with us this morning we do appreciate it  yes we do ambassador i guess you and the  president won't be going to lunch  anytime soon  ambassador bolton no christmas card all  right  thank you sir good to see you
 

